forti-mcp (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Server
    - Initial release of forti-mcp: /usr/bin/forti-mcp, a stdio MCP server
      (JSON-RPC 2.0, MCP 2026-07-28 stateless plus the 2025-11-25 and
      2025-06-18 initialize lifecycle) with the tools forti_discover,
      forti_read, forti_plan and forti_apply over the FortiOS REST API.
    - forti-mcp --version reports what it was built from: the forti-cli engine
      revision and the forti-api version.
  * Packaging
    - The command engine is compiled in statically from forti-cli's source at
      the revision subprojects/forti-cli.wrap pins; no dependency on the
      forti-cli package or the forti executable.
    - Built against the system libforti-api-dev (>= 1.0.1) with
      --wrap-mode=nodownload: the package build fetches nothing.
    - Release build profile: -O3 in place of dpkg's -O2, NDEBUG, and section
      garbage collection (-ffunction-sections -fdata-sections, --gc-sections);
      the network-free unit and e2e suites run against that build unless
      nocheck.
    - amd64 only (vl-release supports one architecture per package contract).

 -- Cooper Larson <cooper@valkyrianlabs.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:29:03 +0000
